      ],
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1209164529260613632"
      ],
      "id": "1209164529260613632",
      "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
      "lang": "en",
      "possibly_sensitive": false,
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 1,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 14,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 0,
        "retweet_count": 1
      },
      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "1209164522964963335",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "Bill's ambition of vision early on:\n\n\"We did BASICs for everything and we knew from the beginning we weren’t the BASIC company. We were going to be a software company.\"\n\nIt is now common for companies to paint a large manifest destiny. But Microsoft was before it was obvious 4/",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1209164529260613632"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "conversation_id": "1209164491943890944",
      "created_at": "2019-12-23T17:31:02.000Z",
      "display_text_range": [
        0,
        273
      ],
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1209164522964963335"
      ],
      "id": "1209164522964963335",
      "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
      "lang": "en",
      "possibly_sensitive": false,
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 2,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 15,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 1,
        "retweet_count": 2
      },
      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "1209164508364591107",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "Bill on competitive inspiration:\n\n\"Our competition said, 'Windows had the risk of just becoming a set of poorly debugged device drivers.' That’s a direct quote, which is great, when your competition motivates you so eloquently. And it was true. That was an actual risk.\" 3/",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1209164522964963335"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "conversation_id": "1209164491943890944",
      "created_at": "2019-12-23T17:30:58.000Z",
      "display_text_range": [
        0,
        280
      ],
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1209164508364591107"
      ],
      "id": "1209164508364591107",
      "in_reply_to_user_id": "615818451",
      "lang": "en",
      "possibly_sensitive": false,
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 1,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 19,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 1,
        "retweet_count": 1
      },
      "referenced_tweets": [
        {
          "id": "1209164491943890944",
          "type": "replied_to"
        }
      ],
      "text": "Bill on IBM as a partner:\n\n\"So if you can pick these toughest customers and meet their needs, then you can sit back and wait. You’re going to be fine. And you have to pick the ones that are highly visible and tough and you can mess up either of those.\"\n\nTough customers matter! 2/",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1209164508364591107"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "conversation_id": "1209164491943890944",
      "created_at": "2019-12-23T17:30:54.000Z",
      "display_text_range": [
        0,
        274
      ],
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1209164491943890944"
      ],
      "entities": {
        "mentions": [
          {
            "end": 33,
            "id": "50393960",
            "start": 23,
            "username": "BillGates"
          },
          {
            "end": 50,
            "id": "10078",
            "start": 38,
            "username": "reidhoffman"
          },
          {
            "end": 68,
            "id": "818902892652466176",
            "start": 53,
            "username": "mastersofscale"
          }
        ]
      },
      "id": "1209164491943890944",
      "lang": "en",
      "possibly_sensitive": false,
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 32,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 126,
        "quote_count": 1,
        "reply_count": 1,
        "retweet_count": 16
      },
      "text": "Incredible quotes from @BillGates and @reidhoffman's @mastersofscale episode:\n\nMitch Lasky on Bill:\n\n“Bill is wrong. But he works so hard, he probably will succeed even though he’s wrong in this case.”\n\nHard work gives you the ability to bend the world in your direction. 1/",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1209164491943890944"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "conversation_id": "1208795031957467136",
      "created_at": "2019-12-22T17:02:48.000Z",
      "display_text_range": [
        0,
        279
      ],
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1208795031957467136"
      ],
      "id": "1208795031957467136",
      "lang": "en",
      "possibly_sensitive": false,
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 1,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 80,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 3,
        "retweet_count": 9
      },
      "text": "Growing up while the smartphone was invented was such a gift.\n\nAs I grew up, all these things that were impossible before became possible, and slowly the whole world came online.\n\nMost of all, I internalized that invention can seem like a toy, but then entirely change the world.",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1208795031957467136"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "conversation_id": "1208218615134052352",
      "created_at": "2019-12-21T02:52:20.000Z",
      "display_text_range": [
        0,
        280
      ],
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1208218615134052352"
      ],
      "id": "1208218615134052352",
      "lang": "en",
      "possibly_sensitive": false,
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 4,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 90,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 1,
        "retweet_count": 6
      },
      "text": "Headed home to New Mexico for the holidays.\n\nLooking back on the year and all its twists and turns, it has been incredible.\n\nThere were many hard fought wins, and even more surprising opportunities disguised as challenges.\n\nThis year was a reminder that the journey is the reward.",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1208218615134052352"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "conversation_id": "1207800076258533376",
      "created_at": "2019-12-19T23:09:12.000Z",
      "display_text_range": [
        0,
        207
      ],
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1207800076258533376"
      ],
      "id": "1207800076258533376",
      "lang": "en",
      "possibly_sensitive": false,
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 11,
        "impression_count": 0,
        "like_count": 100,
        "quote_count": 1,
        "reply_count": 1,
        "retweet_count": 14
      },
      "text": "In the best organizations, it is OK to make mistakes, but unacceptable not to learn from them.\n\nAccomplishing something in a low-information environment is all about accelerating feedback and integrating it.",
      "url": "https://x.com/alexandr_wang/status/1207800076258533376"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "615818451",
      "conversation_id": "1206372099452915712",
      "created_at": "2019-12-16T00:34:56.000Z",
      "display_text_range": [
        0,
        280
      ],
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "1206372099452915712"
